cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the CaRL Library in your research, please cite this software as below."
title: "CaRL Library: Combinatorial Reinforcement Learning for Planning and Imitation"
abstract: |
  The CaRL (Combinatorial Reinforcement Learning) Library is designed for developing and scaling offline and online reinforcement/imitation learning experiments in combinatorial planning problems. It provides tools for environments, data handling, inference, training loops, and AI-guided search algorithms, with support for distributed computation (SLURM, Apptainer), and comes with open-source models and interactive examples.
